course: dictionary
lesson: 8800
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. Sharpness is a good example: it can describe a knife, a photo, a clever mind, a voice or a taste.
explain: In «the sharpness of oranges, tomatoes and fizzy drinks», the sentence is about food, so sharpness means a sour, tangy taste. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: In «the first day with them can feel like someone turned up the sharpness of the whole world», the sentence is about glasses, so sharpness means how clear and detailed things look.
explain: Knives and scissors must be handled carefully because of their sharpness, which is how well their edge can cut.
fact: Sharpness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you talk about some sharpness, not two sharpnesses.
fact: Sharpness means how sharp something is, how well its edge or point can cut or pierce.
fact: Sharpness of a picture or image means how clear and detailed it is.
fact: Sharpness of mind means being quick and clever. Sharpness in someone's voice means it is a bit harsh or cross.
fact: Sharpness can also mean a sour or strong taste, like lemon or strong cheese.
exercise: «Be careful with the sharpness of the kitchen knife.» What does sharpness mean here? | How quick and clever a person is | *How well the blade can cut | How clear a photo looks
exercise: «The sharpness of oranges, tomatoes and fizzy drinks» is in a sentence about food. What does sharpness mean here? | A cutting edge | A harsh, cross voice | Bright, clear colour | *A sour, tangy taste
exercise: «She answered with sharpness in her voice.» What does the sharpness show about her? | She is very sleepy | She is very hungry | *She is a bit cross or harsh | She is singing a song
test: «The first day with glasses can feel like someone turned up the sharpness of the world.» What does sharpness mean here? | *Things look clearer and more detailed | Things are much louder | Things are cut into pieces | Things taste sour
test: Ella says sharpness only means something that cuts. Is she right? | Yes, only knives have sharpness | Yes, but only for scissors | No, sharpness means being slow | *No, sharpness can also mean clever thinking, a clear picture or a sour taste
exam: Which meaning fits «sharpness of mind» best? | *Being quick and clever | Being very hungry | Being wet and grey | Being very old
